														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1494324">
									

<p>The level of detail is very good, especially the footnotes. It makes the entry seem very professional.</p>
<p>However, I'm not sold on the concept. Videogame enemies that become self-aware? An eldritch god that haunts the gamer? This is just too much. And I'm still a little shaky on how the Foundation became aware of the game. One of the junior researchers was intrigued by weird layoffs at an indie game company? Not likely. And how did whatshisname haunt the playtester outside of the game (he claimed to hear the voice even after he left the house)? Not to mention that you fell back into stereotypical videogame-related creepypasta cliches like the melodramatic descriptions of the characters being executed on altars. At least you never claimed that it became &quot;photorealistic&quot;. Ugh. And there is a serious downplay of how the eldritch beastie could have escaped onto the internet. That seems kind of important.</p>
<p>tl;dr Your execution was particularly good, but it doesn't save the entry from the problems in concept and plot.</p>
<p>Downvoted for now, but I'll watch for edits to see if it gets better.</p>

							</div>

								
					
