														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1518080">
									

<p>I actually think that it works precisely <em>because</em> of those elements. Or more to the point, because they aren't actually unexplained. Yes, the game reaches Creepypasta levels of disturbing&#8230;deliberately. Sacrificing a character on an altar is done with the specific intent of the player seeing it, and being disturbed. The game is still functioning within it's intended parameters. What makes it anomalous is the fact that these parameters include trying to disrupt the player, and their mental state. The &quot;demon&quot; isn't really a demon at all. It's an AI that was programmed to behave like a demon, and &quot;takes its role too seriously&quot; so to speak. Anything that happens outside the game, based on test logs, is unlikely to even be resulting directly from the game. The more likely assessment is that, under the constant psychological assault by the system, the tester was driven insane and suffering stress-induced delusions.</p>

