					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1345012&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608063038" alt="kinchtheknifeblade" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1345012)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;" >kinchtheknifeblade</a></span> <span class="odate time_1341002265 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Jun 2012 20:37</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1494348">
									

<p>This is a phenomenal example of the classic &quot;evil videogame&quot; trope used so much in creepypasta. While none of the content is similar, it kind of reminds me of <a href="/scp-1981">SCP-1981</a>, in that it takes this creepypasta trope, puts it into Foundation language, and actually succeeds with the material. This isn't, of course, to say that this article is merely lowly creepypasta or anything like that. I think it rises above the rest, really. This is what videogame creepypastas and SCPs want to be. It isn't merely some ghost trapped in a machine (haha) but it's a progression of really, really good videogame AI.</p>
<p>And I really disagree with ProfessorBlackJack. I don't think it's a literal eldritch god haunting the player, and that's what makes it so wonderful. It's a series of bytes and lines of code programmed to think it was an eldritch god. It is just being the perfect final boss, the best endboss it can be. I think this distinguishes itself from other videogame creepypastas like &quot;Ben Drowned&quot; in that the ending doesn't reveal that it's being haunted by a dead kid or something stupid. This is great, because it's completely rooted in the videogame, and the real horror comes from it being so smart that it begins to infest the computer. It isn't something as dumb as the videogame sucking the player in or killing them. It's great, and I love it. +1.</p>

							</div>

								
