			<div class="content" id="post-content-1494349">
									

<p>Good first effort, Tedly. This isn't bad at all. What keeps me from upvoting, though, is the last part with the eldritch god-horror thing. You did a good job building up the unease with the first part of the article, but then it's BAM- CRAZY HAUNT-GOD. It was a little too over-the-top and felt dissonant.</p>
<p>Most people seem to like this, so I won't tell you to carve up your SCP to fit my personal tastes, but I would rather have seen a test log on some D-Class playing the game, with what the enemies do when they hit the &quot;fucking with the player&quot; phase. Maybe one guy has some deep-seated phobia that the game exploits, while for another guy it references violent acts that they would have committed by reading subtle psychological cues derived from gameplay. And maybe in the last test the game uses actual details from someone's life that there's no way it could have known or accessed.</p>
<p>The person of interest kind of detracts from the mystery for me. I would have preferred the company putting out this extremely weird product and then going under, personnel too obscure to ever be heard from again.</p>

							</div>

								
